The Western blot is essential for confirming an positive ELISA result because it detects antibodies to multiple HIV-1 proteins (e.g., gp160, gp110, C3d-IgG antibodies to C3d-coated antibodies). A positive Western blot requires the presence of at least two bands of the three proteins (gp160, gp110, and C3d).

