- Concentration of sodium fluoride = 0.044% (w/v)
- Volume of dose = 10 mL

First, we need to convert the concentration from weight percent (w/v) to grams per liter (g/L). Since 0.044% (w/v) means 0.044 g of sodium fluoride per 100 mL of solution, we can convert it to grams per liter:

0.044 g/100 mL × (1000 mL/1 L) = 0.044 g/L

Now, we can find the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose:

0.044 g/L × 10 mL × (1 L/1000 mL) = 0.00044 g

Finally, we need to convert the mass from grams to milligrams:

0.00044 g × (1000 mg/1 g) = 0.44 mg

