2. Prognnosis: The stage of the cancer is a important prognostic factor, which is the probability of the cancer occurring again or the patient living for a certain period of time. Patients with cancer that has spread to the lymph nodes have a higher risk of the cancer returning later on than patients with no cancer in the lymph nodes.

