   \[
   \text{Rate} = -\frac{d[NH_4CNO]}{dt} = \frac{d[urea]}{dt} = k[NH_4CNO]^\nu
   \]  
   where \( \nu \) is the order of the reaction.  

   The mass of urea produced is directly proportional to the concentration of the reactants. Thus, the rate of urea formation is proportional to the mass of urea formed.  

