","The correct order of precipitation of sulfides from \( \text{H}_2\text{S} \) gas into a mixture of \( \text{Mn}^{2+}, \text{Ni}^{2+}, \text{Cu}^{2+}, \) and \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) ions in an acidified aqueous solution is as follows:  
1. **\( \text{HgS} \):** \( \text{Hg}^{2+} \) is the most soluble, and \( \text{HgS} \) is the least soluble, precipitating first.  
2. **\( \text{CuS} \):** \( \text{Cu}^{2+} \) is less soluble, and \( \text{CuS} \) is less soluble than \( \text{MnS} \), precipitating after \( \text{HgS} \).  
3. **\( \text{MnS} \):** \( \text{Mn}^{2+} \) is less soluble, and \( \text{MnS} \) is less soluble than \( \text{NiS} \), precipitating after \( \text{CuS} \).  
