</USER_REQUEST>

<ASSISTANT_RESPONSE>
The selectivity factor \( s = k_e / k_m \) is crucial for the amplification of enantiomeric excess (e.e.) in dimerization processes. It quantifies the relative preference for homochiral dimer formation compared to meso dimer formation. The relationship is given by:  
\[
e.e. = \frac{k_e - k_m}{k_e + k_m} = \frac{s - 1}{s + 1}
\]  
