","The sequence is given by $a_1 = (-2015, 14)$ and $a_n - a_{n-1} = (1, 1)$.  
The general form of the sequence is:  
$a_n = a_1 + (n-1)(a_2 - a_1)$.  
Since $a_n - a_{n-1} = (1, 1)$, the sequence is an arithmetic progression with common difference $(1, 1)$.  
The $n$-th vector is:  
$a_n = (-2015, 14) + (n-1)(1, 1) = (-2015 + n - 1, 14 + n - 1) = (-2016 + n, 13 + n)$.  
The magnitude of the $n$-th vector is:  
$\sqrt{(-2016 + n)^2 + (13 + n)^2} = \sqrt{4032256 - 4032n + n^2 + 169 + 26n + n^2} = \2\sqrt{2n^2 - 4006n + 4033925}$.  
