Prove Proposition B.5, which states the following properties for any field \( F \) with elements \( x, y, z \in F \):
1. \( x + z = y + z \) if and only if \( x = y \).
2. If \( z \) is nonzero, then \( x z = y z \) if and only if \( x = y \).
3. If \( x + z = z \), then \( x = 0 \).
4. If \( x z = z \) and \( z \neq 0 \), then \( x = 1 \).
5. \( 0 \cdot x = 0 \), \( (-1) \cdot x = -x \), and \( (-1) \cdot (-1) = 1 \).
6. If \( x y = 0 \), then \( x = 0 \) or \( y = 0 \).<end_of_turn>
