The negation of "" $A \cup B = A \)."" is "" $A \cup B \neq A \)..""

The negation of "" $A \cap B = B \)."" is "" $A \cap B \neq B \)..""

Thus, the negation of "" If $A \cup B = A$, then $A \cap B = B$ "" is "" $A \cup B = A\) and \(A \cap B \neq B\)"".

Thus, the negation is:
\[
\neg (A \cup B = A) \vee \neg (A \cap B = B)
\]
