\]

where \( 2^n \leq x \). When \( n = \lfloor \log_{2}(x) \rfloor \), the term \( 2^n N(x/2^n) \) becomes \( 2^n N(1) = 0 \) (since \( N(1) = 0 \). The sum becomes \( \sum_{i=0}^{n-1} 2^i = 2^n - 1 \).

