The index of refraction \( n \) is defined as the ratio of the speed of light in a vacuum \( c \) to the speed of light in the medium \( v \):
\[
n = \frac{c}{v}
\]
Given that the speed of light in the plastic is 0.680 times the speed of light in a vacuum:
\[
v = 0.680c
\]
Substituting this into the formula:
\[
n = \frac{c}{0.680c} = \frac{1}{0.680} \approx 1.47
\]
