   The gravitational force \( F \) provides the centripetal force:  
   \[
   F = ma = \frac{mv^2}{r}
   \]  
   Given \( F = 3600 \, \text{N} \), we can rearrange to solve for \( r \):  
   \[
   r = \frac{mv^2}{F}
   \]  
